# public/_redirects
# Order matters. Netlify evaluates top to bottom and stops at the first match.
# Static files (assets, fonts, favicons, robots.txt, sitemap.xml, llms.txt,
# 410.html) are served before any non-forced rule, so they need no entries.
# Netlify limits: wildcards only at the END of a path (/solar-* is invalid),
# a 410 must point at a file that exists (public/410.html) or it is served as
# a 404, and a trailing slash cannot be added or removed by a rule.
# Every new route must be added here, to routes.json and to sitemap.xml
# together: npm run check:routes enforces it.

# 1. Canonical host — must be the first rule
https://itlegends.co.za/*  https://www.itlegends.co.za/:splat  301!

# 2. Canonical root — /index.html is one of the duplicate URLs in GSC.
#    Forced, or the real index.html file would shadow this rule.
/index.html  /  301!

# 3. Retired WooCommerce and solar URL space — HTTP 410 Gone (D45).
#    Confirmed in the GSC not-indexed export and the prerender log.
#    Bare and wildcard forms are both listed: a splat is not guaranteed to
#    match the parent path itself.
/shop                       /410.html  410
/shop/*                     /410.html  410
/product                    /410.html  410
/product/*                  /410.html  410
/product-category           /410.html  410
/product-category/*         /410.html  410
/cart                       /410.html  410
/cart/*                     /410.html  410
/solar-inverters            /410.html  410
/solar-inverters/*          /410.html  410
/solar-charge-controllers   /410.html  410
/solar-charge-controllers/* /410.html  410

